      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "After oral administration of radiolabelled metamizol to rats, drug-related material reached 15 µg/g in brain, confirming systemic-to-brain penetration in the same chemical family.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The closest and most direct evidence from antipyrine/dipyrone metabolites consistently shows meaningful CNS access in human CSF, rat microdialysis, and oral brain uptake; lower-similarity fail records are outweighed.",
